        }, {
          "title" : "Managing requests to modify user accounts",
          "props" : [ {
            "name" : "sort-id",
            "value" : "catalog[1].group[08].group[1].group[05]"
          } ],
          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "Requests to modify user accounts, such as resetting a password, changing a mobile phone number or email address, temporarily disabling multi-factor authentication, or re-enrolling for multi-factor authentication, could indicate a malicious actor attempting to conduct a help desk attack.\n\nIn dealing with such situations, personnel should have clear guidance to think critically before actioning unusual requests as well as a process to report threatening demands for immediate action, pressure for secrecy or requests to circumvent normal business processes and procedures."
