        "parts" : [ {
          "name" : "overview",
          "prose" : "# Context\n\nThis section describes the hardening of privately owned and organisation-owned mobile devices, such as smartphones and tablets that use a mobile operating system. Alternatively, guidance for privately owned and organisation-owned mobile devices that use a desktop operating system is available in the ‘Operating system hardening’ section of the [Guidelines for system hardening](#de7525f3-a466-40a5-abdd-3ae24a6d1b44).\n\n# Further information\n\nFurther information on cyber supply chain risk management can be found in the ‘Cyber supply chain risk management’ section of the [Guidelines for procurement and outsourcing](#f37a4848-0791-4870-b316-5536c2681c28).\n\nFurther information on evaluated products can be found in the ‘Evaluated product procurement’ section of the [Guidelines for evaluated products](#a699a3aa-828d-479b-b50b-98127bb19437).\n\nFurther information on Common Criteria Protection Profiles for mobile devices can be found in the following United States’ National Information Assurance Partnership publications:\n\n- [Protection Profile for Mobile Device Management Version 4.0](#ed6aa6ab-545d-48eb-92bc-9ad763d4b868)\n- [Protection Profile for Mobile Device Fundamentals Version 3.3](#f160b04e-1a32-4dd5-816e-1cba8c97982c).\n\nFurther information on hardening mobile platforms can be found in the following ASD publications:\n\n- [Security configuration guide: Apple iOS 14 devices](#d2910e61-da88-4d29-b860-83c25161fd18)\n- [Security configuration guide: Samsung Galaxy S10, S20 and Note 20 devices](#616fce77-495b-472a-a552-7593ab64f188)\n- [Security configuration guide: Viasat Mobile Dynamic Defense](#daae37ef-262f-4b20-bfb7-a27901f3c2db).\n\nFurther information on encrypting mobile devices and their communications can be found in the ‘Cryptographic fundamentals’ section of the [Guidelines for cryptography](#195abe87-bb1e-4006-8b42-eaecca4d51f1)."
        } ],
        "groups" : [ {
          "title" : "Mobile device management policy",
          "props" : [ {
            "name" : "sort-id",
            "value" : "catalog[1].group[11].group[2].group[1]"
          } ],
          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "Since mobile devices routinely leave the office environment, and the protection it affords, it is important that a mobile device management policy is developed, implemented and maintained to ensure that mobile devices are sufficiently hardened. In doing so, it is important that Mobile Device Management solutions that have completed a Common Criteria evaluation against the Protection Profile for Mobile Device Management, version 4.0 or later, are used to enforce mobile device management policy."
