          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "When sanitising printers and MFDs, the printer cartridge or MFD print drum should be sanitised in addition to the removal or sanitisation of any media. This can be achieved by printing random text with no blank areas on each colour printer cartridge or MFD print drum. In addition, image transfer rollers and platens can become imprinted with text and images over time and should be destroyed if any text or images have been retained. Finally, any paper jammed in the paper path should be removed.\n\nWhen printer cartridges and MFD print drums cannot be sanitised due to a hardware failure, or when they are empty, there is no other option but to destroy them. Printer ribbons cannot be sanitised and should be destroyed."
