          "title" : "Operating system releases and versions",
          "props" : [ {
            "name" : "sort-id",
            "value" : "catalog[1].group[15].group[1].group[02]"
          } ],
          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "Newer releases of operating systems often introduce improvements in security functionality. This can make it more difficult for malicious actors to craft reliable exploits for vulnerabilities they discover. Using older releases of operating systems, especially those no longer supported by vendors, may expose an organisation to vulnerabilities or exploitation techniques that have since been mitigated. In addition, 64-bit versions of operating systems support additional security functionality that legacy 32-bit versions do not."
          } ],
