          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "Newer releases of server applications often introduce improvements in security functionality. This can make it more difficult for malicious actors to craft reliable exploits for vulnerabilities they discover. In addition, using older releases of server applications, especially those no longer supported by vendors, may expose an organisation to vulnerabilities or exploitation techniques that have since been mitigated. This is particularly important for internet-facing server applications."
