          "title" : "Insecure authentication methods",
          "props" : [ {
            "name" : "sort-id",
            "value" : "catalog[1].group[16].group[1].group[16]"
          } ],
          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "Authentication methods need to resist theft, interception, duplication, forgery, unauthorised access and unauthorised modification. For example, LAN Manager authentication protects credentials with a weak hashing algorithm, while all versions of NT LAN Manager lack mutual authentication and rely on password-derived hashes. As such, malicious actors can exploit these authentication methods via relay attacks, pass-the-hash attacks and the offline cracking of captured authentication exchanges. Instead, an organisation should use Kerberos for authentication within Microsoft Windows environments."
          } ],
